# TradeFix: Premium UI

TradeFix is a **premium SaaS for paying traders**. UI work is judged at a high-end product bar, not an MVP sketch.

## Before any UI change

- Study the existing layout, spacing scale, typography, and neighboring cards first.
- Match current dashboard language: `dash-card`, shared header height, consistent padding, thin borders, no heavy shadows.
- If the user provides a sketch or reference, treat it as the layout contract (column widths, row structure). Do not invent a different grid.

## Hard visual rules

- Cards in the same row **must share top edge, bottom edge, and header height**. Use stretch/`h-full`, not `items-start` with uneven content.
- Titles, tabs, and toolbars in a row use the **same header height** (e.g. `h-11`). Never leave one card untitled so the chart drops.
- Gutters, padding, and radius stay consistent across a row. No leftover footer on one card that makes it taller.
- Charts: profit **green**, loss **red**. Brand purple is for chrome (nav, buttons, score), not P&L.
- Responsive: desktop grid first; on small screens stack cleanly; never crush a calendar/table — scroll inside the card if needed.

## Do not ship

- Misaligned cards, uneven heights, clipped dropdowns, cramped cells, leftover purple P&L bars, or “close enough” spacing.
- Extra chrome the user did not ask for (sidebars, filters, extra buttons) when they asked for one component.

## After UI work

- Re-check every surface that shares the layout (dashboard, day view, calendar).
- If you cannot verify in a browser, say so. Do not call the UI done from a single screenshot in your head.
